  "matching": "Ground truth is the glyph ink box of each labelled span (pixel difference between the screen and the same screen with that text made transparent). A target is a hit when one unmatched detection of the same kind covers at least 90% of the ink box area and is no larger than 8x that area (so a full-screen mask cannot score). Matching is one-to-one; duplicate boxes and wrong-kind predictions count as false positives. Recall at IoU >= 0.5 against the ink box is reported alongside as a stricter localisation measure. A hard-negative span is a false positive when an unmatched detection covers at least 30% of it.",
